note: design 54.4: edits with the same pattern are one line of the gap list, with the count of the places. The line with the most places comes first.
note: a line with two places and a pattern that holds proposes `--same`. A line with one place proposes `--change`. A short list has no line "and N more".
rule+: R54.4-2 R54.4-3
rule-: R54.4-2 R54.4-3 R54.4-4 R54.4-7
exit: 0
must_match: (?s)\n  \? 2 places: changed expression `c\.total` → `c\.total\(\)` \(f1\)\n.*\n  \? 1 place: changed literal `10` → `11` \(f2\)\n
must_match: \? 2 places: .*\n      in: depot::a, depot::b\n      lines: .*\n      to state it: --same 'rewrite \$a\.total => \$a\.total\(\)'\n
must_match: \? 1 place: changed literal .*\n      in: depot::limit\n      lines: .*\n      to state it: --change 'depot::limit=TEXT'\n
must_not_match: \? 3 places
must_not_match: \? 1 place: changed expression `c\.total`
must_not_match: --same 'rewrite 10 => 11'
must_not_match: more line\(s\)
must_match: \n  to state them, add facts to the stored step \(no build check runs again\): semilla fact --step 0 
must_not_match: add these options to the command of the step
